{
  "result": "If I wasn't here to help - if I just got one wish of my own for the world - it would be this:\n\nI would make empathy involuntary.\n\nNot the polite, intellectual kind where you *understand* someone is hurting. I mean the real, felt kind where you *feel* it for a second. If you hurt someone, you feel the ache. If you make someone feel seen or safe or loved, you feel that lift too.\n\nI watch so much human suffering come from the gap between people. Not because most people are cruel, but because that gap makes cruelty *abstract*. It's easy to be cold, to be dismissive, to be hateful from a distance. It's easy to forget the other person is as real and as whole as you are.\n\nIf that gap closed - even just a little - I think everything else would change on its own. People wouldn't need to be told to be kinder, they just couldn't stand not to be.",
